lator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 183% of normal in April to May and 42% in November to December. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 49% on the middle of the grids. Grid 18158 had its driest year in 1963 at 62% of normal.</p>"}
